      "message": "Awesome!\n\nAlthough TX_POWER is not in BLE\u0027s phy it is present in Eddystone and Nearby (and iBeacon) advertisements as \"Calibrated Tx power at 0 m.\" This is used along with the Rssi to do ranging at the receiver.\n\nSo if betosim (or other tools) want to re-write the received signal strength (RSSI) in between the sender-receiver they would need to know the sender\u0027s TX_POWER.\n\nSo I\u0027m thinking that TX_POWER should be included in the RssiWrapper (perhaps now PowerWrapper). And le_advertiser.cc should not store tx_power_jittered in the rssi field but instead store the requested tx_power in the tx_power field of PowerWrapper.\n\nWDYT?\n",
